    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. For q-124958 and q-124959, the Pythagorean identity gives magnitudes sqrt(15)/4 and sqrt(11)/6; quadrant II makes sine positive and cosine negative. For q-42043, quadrant II gives cosine −sqrt(3)/2, hence tangent −sqrt(3)/3. For q-85640, quadrant IV gives sine −3sqrt(5)/7, hence cotangent −2sqrt(5)/15. For q-85643 and q-125004, quadrant II gives cosines −2sqrt(6)/7 and −sqrt(15)/8; their reciprocals are −7sqrt(6)/12 and −8sqrt(15)/15. The statistics solutions explicitly use population variance: q-87464 has mean −3 and squared deviations totaling 74, giving 37/3; q-87612 has mean 3 and mean square 97/7, giving standard deviation sqrt(34/7); q-87613 has mean 4 and mean square 124/5, giving sqrt(44/5). The chain rule gives q-48658 derivative 3e^(5−x), whose requested value is 6; q-48007 derivative −8e^(4x−1); q-107445 derivative (2x−2)e^(x²−2x); q-107452 derivative (3x²−4)e^(x³−4x), whose value at 2 is 8; and q-107461 derivative −4·6^(1−4x)ln(6). Finally, q-101604 gives −9/x, and q-17392 gives derivative 2e·x^(e−1)−1/x, whose value at 1 is 2e−1. Each quotation below is a verbatim answer-bearing span from that question's supplied solution. No submitted grades or earlier answers were supplied.",
